      "side": 1,
      "message": "And if you want more readability we might want to replace the input of data \u0026 size pair with `absl::Span` or `base::Span` or `std::span`, but the first two require extra dependency, and the third one requires the C++20.\n\nYou should write down what is the style you want as a guide, make sure everything in it is doable(e.g. we don\u0027t support `absl` \u0026 `base` \u0026 C++20/23).\nAnd clarified what C/C++ features are recommended / banned. \n(e.g. Using std::vector\u003cuint_8\u003e when possible, or static size array, or data size pair, or std::string, or C style array, std::span...)\n\nThe idea of changing the coding conventions should not be popped up one by one in the code review process.",
