      "message": "This function signature\n```\nstd::optional\u003cstruct fp_elliptic_curve_public_key\u003e \nencrypt_data_with_ecdh_key_in_place(\n    const struct fp_elliptic_curve_public_key \u0026in_pubkey,\n    uint8_t *data, size_t data_size, uint8_t *iv, size_t iv_size)\n```\ndoesn\u0027t make the code clearer to read.\n\nBecause those three output parameters(`out_pubkey` \u0026 `data` \u0026 `iv`) have the same importance. Only putting one of them in the return value is weird.\n\nAnd packing them together will require the decision of vector/array/raw buffer.",
